hed (1.2.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * repl(1): add -l/--line to expand match to entire line (default: matched only).
  * repl(1): add -g/--global (default) and -1/--first for occurrence control.
  * repl(1): add --range=N..M to replace N-th through M-th occurrences per line.
  * repl(1): line-based replacement logic with occurrence counting.
  * insert(1): fix -r behavior at prepend: -0 -r3 removes 2 lines (keep from line 3),
    -1 -r3 removes 3 lines (keep from line 4), consistent with 1-based indexing.
  * insert: update man page to clarify -r behavior difference between -0 and -1.
  * catq: anothor cat but silently ignore missing filenames.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:48:00 +0800

hed (1.1.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * repl(1): add -n/--dryrun to preview changes without rewriting files;
    with -u/-c still print patches but leave targets untouched.
  * repl: custom patch banner "::: FILE :::" instead of diff temp-path
    ---/+++ headers; --color[=WHEN] and --palette=PALETTE (GNU diff style)
    highlight the banner (background/reverse) and added/deleted lines.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:30:00 +0800

hed (1.0.0) testing; urgency=medium

  * insert(1): in-place line splicing with extended/string/filename sources,
    digit position options (-0..-9, -n, -a, -p), trailing --blank defaults,
    EOF padding, and -r/--remove for delete/update operations.
  * insert: empty delete at prepend (-0/-p/-1 -rN) keeps from 1-based line N
    without adding a trailing blank (e.g. insert -0 -r3 on a/b/c/d/e => c/d/e).
  * repl(1): batch in-place replace with fixed/POSIX/PCRE2 patterns, grep-like
    file selection, binary handling, and diff/summary reporting.
  * Standalone insert and repl binaries (no shared libhed).
  * gettext UI translations (de, eo, fr, it, ja, ko, th, vi, zh_CN, zh_TW).
  * Translated man pages for insert(1) and repl(1) in the same languages.
  * Check-based unit and CLI integration tests.

 -- Lenik (谢继雷) <lenik@bodz.net>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 14:40:00 +0800
